# %% [markdown]
# # Q7 — does the serving stack change the answer, or only the number? (secondary)
#
# The paper's headline numbers come from six models served **locally** (vLLM /
# `transformers`, on-premises GPUs). The same six models are also available
# through OpenRouter's `:free` tier, an API-served stack, on the `base` image
# variant only. This notebook is not a search for the more accurate pathway —
# it is not one, in any way that survives being stated plainly. It asks a
# narrower and more useful question: **can the API number be regenerated by
# anyone who did not run it themselves?**
#
# **The argument in one paragraph, so the tables below are read the right way
# round.** The two serving pathways return different values on about half of
# 27,720 matched responses. Overall MAE improves through the API for three of
# the six models, so this is not a story about one pathway being worse. What
# makes the local pathway the one this study reports is that it is
# **specified**: framework, precision and hardware are recorded, and
# re-running the protocol reproduced 100 of 100 responses exactly for five of
# six models. OpenRouter's `:free` tier discloses neither the quantization,
# the model revision nor the decoding parameters behind a given call, and any
# of them may change between requests without notice. A number produced
# through the API cannot be regenerated, because the system that produced it
# is not specified — a researcher calling the same endpoint next year is not
# running the same experiment and has no way to tell whether they are. **This
# is a claim about reproducibility, not about accuracy, and the tables below
# are read that way throughout: a smaller API overall MAE is not a point in
# the API's favour, it is one more number nobody else can reproduce.**
#
# **What this comparison can and cannot conclude.** Local memory footprints
# recorded during the local runs are consistent with bf16 weights at each
# model's parameter count, so the local side sits on a known footing. The API
# side does not: nothing in this repository establishes what precision,
# quantization or model revision OpenRouter served. Any disagreement between
# the two pathways below is therefore never attributed to the serving stack
# alone — it could be the stack, the weights, or both, and no test here can
# separate them. Every claim in this notebook is worded "stack and possibly
# weights", and a close agreement is read the same way in reverse: evidence
# the two *behave* similarly, never evidence they run identical weights.
#
# Two further constraints bind everything below. **No API latency claim of
# any kind** — the API run hit rate limits and retried, so its latency
# measures rate-limiting and retry timing, not inference speed, and is not
# analysed here. **API confidence is not compared to local confidence**, and
# no API confidence claim is made for Llama-4-Maverick, whose API confidence
# value is 42% exactly 1.0. **No campaign-clustered companion is computed
# anywhere in this notebook** — the three campaigns are diverse by design and
# cannot support a dependable cluster-robust interval with only three clusters.

# %% [markdown]
# ## Setup
#
# The seed is fixed so every resample below is reproducible.
#
# **RNG discipline.** Every bootstrap quantity below draws from its own
# generator, seeded from `SEED` plus a fixed integer offset recorded next to
# its declaration: isolating each quantity's draws means adding or removing
# one bootstrap elsewhere in this notebook cannot silently move a number
# already read from another part. **Point estimates are deterministic
# functions of the loaded data and are asserted against fixed published
# values** — this cell fails if any of them moves, so a change to the
# analysis cannot silently invalidate the manuscript. Interval endpoints are
# not asserted against a fixed value, because a bootstrap interval's exact
# endpoints depend on the draw sequence and are expected to vary slightly
# from run to run; the assertions below check the interval excludes or
# includes zero where the reported conclusion depends on that, not its exact
# bounds.

# %%
